/-!
# Finite limits and colimits of finite étale covers

Source: literature/blueprint/master/blueprint/sec-curve-estimates/sk-prop-h2/
lem-fet-finite-limits.md (blueprint: lem-fet-finite-limits).
The statement is unchanged in the main-20261015 blueprint, at the same relative path.
Proof route: Stacks, pione.tex, Tag 0BN9 (lemma-finite-etale-covers-limits-colimits).
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.FiniteEtale

/-- Finite étale covers have finite limits and finite colimits, and arbitrary base change
preserves both. Source: blueprint, `sec-curve-estimates/sk-prop-h2/lem-fet-finite-limits.md`
(blueprint: lem-fet-finite-limits); Stacks, pione.tex, Tag 0BN9.

Proof:
1. A morphism `P → R` of finite étale `Y`-schemes is finite
   (`lem-weil-pbc-finite-permanence-over-separated`, as `R → Y` is finite hence separated)
   and étale (clause (3) of `lem-weil-pbc-etale-composition-cancellation`).
2. The identity of `Y` is finite étale and terminal. For a cospan `P → R ← Q` the scheme
   fibre product `P ×_R Q` (`def-pc-fibre-product`) is finite étale over `Y` by step 1,
   base change, `lem-weil-pbc-finite-composition` and
   `lem-weil-pbc-etale-composition-cancellation`; it is the pullback in `FÉt(Y)`.
3. For `g : Y' → Y`, `Y ×_Y Y' ≅ Y'` and
   `(P ×_R Q) ×_Y Y' ≅ (P ×_Y Y') ×_{R ×_Y Y'} (Q ×_Y Y')` compatibly with projections, so
   `g^*` preserves the terminal object and pullbacks;
   `lem-weil-pbc-finite-limits-from-terminal-pullbacks` gives finite limits and their
   preservation by `g^*`.
4. Finite coproducts are disjoint unions (`lem-weil-pbc-scheme-coproduct-family`), finite by
   `lem-weil-pbc-finite-coproduct` and étale by `lem-sc-etale-coproduct-etale`; the empty
   scheme is the initial object. Base change preserves them
   (`lem-sc-etale-fibre-product-base-change-coproduct`), including the empty one.
5. For parallel arrows `a, b : Z ⇉ P`, `lem-weil-pbc-finite-etale-etale-local-split` at each
   point (applied to `P`, then to the pullback of `Z`) gives an étale covering `{U_i → Y}` with
   `P_{U_i} = ∐_{S_i} U_i` and `Z_{U_i} = ∐_{T_i} U_i`, `S_i, T_i` finite; no common
   cardinality over all `i` is asserted.
6. Refining by opens (intersections of the finitely many clopen partitions given by the
   inverse images of target sheets), both arrows are induced by maps `α_i, β_i : T_i → S_i`.
7. On one member `U`, put `E = S_i/∼` for the relation generated by `α_i t ∼ β_i t`,
   `Q_i = ∐_E U` and `q_i : P_U → Q_i` sheet-wise. By the sections description of maps out of
   a disjoint union, `q_i` is a coequalizer among all `U`-schemes, and stays one after any
   base change `V → U`.
8. With `U = ∐ U_i → Y` (surjective étale) and `Q' = ∐ Q_i`, `Q' → U` is finite étale
   (`lem-weil-pbc-finite-local-on-target`, clause (3)). Gluing on the small étale site
   (`lem-weil-pbc-small-etale-representable-presheaf-sheaf`,
   `lem-weil-pbc-etale-covering-base-change`) gives `q' : P_U → Q'`, a coequalizer
   universally under base change.
9. Over `U ×_Y U` the two pullbacks of `q'` coequalize the same pair, giving a unique
   isomorphism `φ` with the cocycle and identity conditions: `(Q', φ)` is a finite étale
   descent datum and `q'` a morphism of descent data.
10. `lem-galois-descent` for `u : U → Y` descends `(Q', φ)` to `Q` and `q'` to
    `q : P → Q` with `q a = q b`; full faithfulness descends the factorizations of step 8,
    so `q` is a coequalizer in `FÉt(Y)`.
11. For arbitrary `g : Y' → Y`, `U ×_Y Y' → Y'` is surjective étale
    (`lem-weil-pbc-etale-covering-base-change`); `g^* q` is locally a base change of `q'`,
    hence locally a coequalizer, and `lem-galois-descent` over `Y'` gives the unique global
    factorization. So `g^*` preserves coequalizers.
12. A finite diagram `D` (`def-galois-finite-limits-colimits`) has colimit the coequalizer of
    `∐_{f : i → j} D(i) ⇉ ∐_i D(i)`, including the empty diagram. By steps 4 and 11, `g^*`
    preserves this presentation, hence finite colimits. With step 3 this is exactness in the
    sense of `def-galois-exact-functor`. -/
theorem finite_limits_colimits_and_exact_baseChange (Y : Scheme.{u}) :
    HasFiniteLimits Y.FiniteEtale ∧ HasFiniteColimits Y.FiniteEtale ∧
      ∀ (Y' : Scheme.{u}) (f : Y' ⟶ Y),
        PreservesFiniteLimits (pullback f) ∧ PreservesFiniteColimits (pullback f) := by
  sorry

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.FiniteEtale
